From 3e71c1e1eda0729e9074b9e461dcbc17354eb53d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:57:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 103/109] fix(classifier): say why a model dir is refused, and
 probe et/ort for the image route

Review round 2 of B204.

A manifest.json that resolves inside the model dir but is not a regular
file (a directory, a symlink to one, a FIFO) counted as absent, so text
sidecars made the dir a text model. It is now an invalid declaration like
the other unreadable cases.

Every refusal now carries its reason: manifest escapes the model dir,
cannot be resolved (an escape and an unresolvable path are told apart),
is not a regular file, is over 1 MiB, is not a JSON object, or declares
image-classification with an unusable labels_file; or the labels file
escapes, cannot be resolved or is not a regular file. lemond logs each
refused dir once as a WARNING ("Not a model: <dir>: <reason>"), and a load
whose candidates were all refused fails with those reasons instead of "no
servable model directory".

et-server and ort-server report no task on /health, so an engine without
POST /classify/image used to load an image model and then 404 on every
request. Their image loads now send an image request without an image: an
engine with the route refuses it with a 400, one without it answers with
cpp-httplib's default 404 (empty body), and the load is then refused,
naming the binary and the release that has the route. A route-not-found
404 at request time (an engine replaced after the load) becomes a 502
image_classification_unsupported with the same text; any other engine 404
passes through. tflite keeps its /health task check, gets no probe and no
404 rewrite. The per-engine text lives once, as kImageRouteRequirement in
each descriptor header.

Engine evidence (gh api repos/<repo>/contents/src/main.cpp?ref=<tag>,
counting "/classify/image"):
- ianbmacdonald/et-server v0.1.0: 0; v0.2.0: 3. So et-server v0.2.0.
- ianbmacdonald/ort-server v0.1.2-musl: 0; v0.2.0-musl: 3.
- lemonade-sdk/ort-server 0.4.0 (the default download in
  backend_versions.json): 0. So an onnxruntime image model needs cpu_bin
  set to ianbmacdonald/ort-server v0.2.0-musl or later.
None of those main.cpp files installs a 404 handler, so the missing route
gets cpp-httplib's default empty-body 404.

classify() on a backend with nothing loaded now refuses with the same
"no classification model is loaded" message as classify_image().

Tests: test_classifier_layout checks each reason and the non-regular
manifest cases on all three engines, and that a backend with nothing
loaded refuses both routes. server_image_classify.py: test_517 (et/ort
loads refused by the probe, tflite's 404 passed through), test_517b (the
502 fallback, via the fake's FAKE_IMAGE_ROUTE_GONE), and test_518 now
requires /pull 200 and the reason in the /load error, and removes what it
wrote. The fake's FAKE_NO_IMAGE_ROUTE answers with an empty 404 like
cpp-httplib.

